% Test cases for the hospital beds policy (hospital_beds.le): synthetic
% claims, one or two per criterion of LCD L33820 and per payment condition
% of dmepos.le. Findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's (the
% clinical note) or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer
% conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query,
% so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary,
% and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base hospital beds cases includes these resources:
    hospital_beds.

the knowledge base hospital beds cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a semi-electric bed (E0260): the
% positioning finding, the frequent-changes finding, and every documentation
% requirement in the record. E0260 is not on the CMS face-to-face list: the
% order need only reach the supplier before the date of service.
scenario semi_electric_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0260".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "severe pain from metastatic bone disease is relieved only with the knees and trunk elevated".
    the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the hospital bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the hospital bed includes order date.
    the order for the hospital bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the hospital bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the hospital bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the hospital bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the hospital bed was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the hospital bed.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A fixed height bed (E0290, on the CMS face-to-face and WOPD list) by
% criterion 3: the head of the bed elevated 45 degrees most of the time for
% congestive heart failure; the face-to-face encounter within six months
% before the order, the order communicated before delivery.
scenario fixed_height_head_elevation_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0290".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ben requires the head of the bed elevated 45 degrees most of the time.
    the medical record of Ben documents congestive heart failure.
    the treating practitioner examined Ben for the hospital bed in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the hospital bed is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the hospital bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the hospital bed includes order date.
    the order for the hospital bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the hospital bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the hospital bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the hospital bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the hospital bed was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the hospital bed.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The head elevated 20 degrees only, for the same condition: criterion 3
% fails; nothing records a positioning finding, so the answer is conditional
% on that judgment alone.
scenario fixed_height_low_elevation is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0250".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ben.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ben requires the head of the bed elevated 20 degrees most of the time.
    the medical record of Ben documents congestive heart failure.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Ben is established"].

% The head elevated 45 degrees for a condition the LCD does not name, and
% the positioning finding rejected on review: criterion 3 fails and no
% judgment is open.
scenario fixed_height_unlisted_condition is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0250".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ben requires the head of the bed elevated 45 degrees most of the time.
    the medical record of Ben documents gastroesophageal reflux.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Ben is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the note describes no positioning an ordinary bed cannot provide".
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A fixed height bed by criterion 4: traction equipment.
scenario fixed_height_traction is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0251".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Cy requires traction equipment that can only be attached to a hospital bed.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A variable height bed (E0255): a fixed height criterion and the transfer
% finding.
scenario variable_height is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0255".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "contractures of both hips require the legs elevated and the trunk supported".
    the finding needs variable height for transfers about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "transfers to the wheelchair are possible only with the bed lowered to seat height".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The same bed with the transfer finding rejected: not reasonable and
% necessary.
scenario variable_height_transfers_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0255".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding needs variable height for transfers about Dee is unsupported, according to the medical reviewer, because "the beneficiary is bedbound and does not transfer".
    rn expects answers [].

% A semi-electric bed for a beneficiary about whom nothing says the body
% position must change frequently: the answer is conditional on that
% finding.
scenario semi_electric_no_frequent_changes is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0261".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Eve is established"].

% A total electric bed (E0265) with every finding: never covered.
scenario total_electric is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0265".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Eve.
    the residence of Eve is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding needs variable height for transfers about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% A heavy duty extra wide bed (E0301) for a beneficiary of 300 pounds: under
% the 350-pound threshold.
scenario heavy_duty_under_weight is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0301".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Fay is 300 pounds.
    rn expects answers [].

% Weight classes: a 650-pound beneficiary is outside the heavy duty class
% (E0301, at most 600 pounds) and inside the extra heavy duty class (E0304).
% E0304 is on the CMS face-to-face and WOPD list: the complete file of the
% second claim is payable.
scenario weight_class is:
    claim 1 is for the heavy duty bed.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty bed is "E0301".
    the heavy duty bed is furnished to Gus.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    claim 2 is for the extra heavy duty bed.
    the HCPCS code of the extra heavy duty bed is "E0304".
    the extra heavy duty bed is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-04-10.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the residence of Gus is private residence.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the weight of Gus is 650 pounds.
    the treating practitioner examined Gus for the extra heavy duty bed in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-02-01.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed includes order date.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the extra heavy duty bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the extra heavy duty bed was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the extra heavy duty bed.
    pay expects answers ["claim 2 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The third rental month of the semi-electric bed: continued need and
% continued use documented within the preceding twelve months.
scenario rental_month_3 is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0260".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 3.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the hospital bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the hospital bed includes order date.
    the order for the hospital bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the hospital bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the hospital bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the hospital bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the hospital bed was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the hospital bed.
    the medical record documents continued need for the hospital bed on 2026-05-20.
    the record documents continued use of the hospital bed on 2026-05-20.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The same third month without a record of continued use: reasonable and
% necessary, not payable. The flip's one change is to drop the rental month
% (an initial claim needs no continued-use record): the record it lacks is
% dated, and the rules leave the date open, so adding it is not a candidate
% change.
scenario rental_month_3_no_continued_use is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0260".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 3.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the hospital bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the hospital bed includes order date.
    the order for the hospital bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the hospital bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the hospital bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the hospital bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the hospital bed was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the hospital bed.
    the medical record documents continued need for the hospital bed on 2026-05-20.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["remove: the rental month of claim 1 is 3"]].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy, and the flip adds the missing proof.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0260".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-04-10.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed is dated 2026-02-15.
    the order for the hospital bed is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the hospital bed includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the hospital bed includes order date.
    the order for the hospital bed includes description of the item.
    the order for the hospital bed includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the hospital bed includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the hospital bed was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-16.
    the hospital bed was delivered on 2026-04-10.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the hospital bed"]].

% The Council finds the record does not show positioning an ordinary bed
% cannot provide: the claim is not reasonable and necessary.
scenario council_positioning_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0260".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the finding positioning infeasible in ordinary bed about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the physician's statement that the beneficiary needs the head elevated does not describe a condition, its severity or its frequency, and an ordinary bed with pillows elevates the head".
    the finding needs frequent changes in body position about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Accessories: a trapeze bar (E0910) for a beneficiary who needs it to get
% in and out of bed; a heavy duty trapeze (E0911) for a 200-pound
% beneficiary (under 250); a trapeze bar used on an ordinary bed; side rails
% (E0305) added to a bed that meets the fixed height criteria.
scenario accessories is:
    claim 1 is for the trapeze bar.
    the HCPCS code of the trapeze bar is "E0910".
    the trapeze bar is furnished to Ida.
    claim 2 is for the heavy duty trapeze bar.
    the HCPCS code of the heavy duty trapeze bar is "E0911".
    the heavy duty trapeze bar is furnished to Ida.
    claim 3 is for the ordinary bed trapeze bar.
    the HCPCS code of the ordinary bed trapeze bar is "E0910".
    the ordinary bed trapeze bar is furnished to Ida.
    the ordinary bed trapeze bar is used on an ordinary bed.
    claim 4 is for the side rails.
    the HCPCS code of the side rails is "E0305".
    the side rails is furnished to Ida.
    the side rails is an accessory of the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0291".
    the hospital bed is furnished to Ida.
    the finding needs trapeze about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "cannot get in or out of bed without pulling up".
    the finding side rails required about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    Ida requires traction equipment that can only be attached to a hospital bed.
    the weight of Ida is 200 pounds.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A replacement foam mattress (E0272) for a beneficiary owned hospital bed,
% and a bed cradle (E0280).
scenario mattress_and_cradle is:
    claim 1 is for the mattress.
    the HCPCS code of the mattress is "E0272".
    the mattress is furnished to Jo.
    the mattress is an accessory of the hospital bed.
    the HCPCS code of the hospital bed is "E0250".
    the hospital bed is owned by the beneficiary.
    claim 2 is for the bed cradle.
    the HCPCS code of the bed cradle is "E0280".
    the bed cradle is furnished to Jo.
    the finding replacement mattress required about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the mattress is worn through and the beneficiary has a stage 2 pressure ulcer".
    the finding bed cradle necessary about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "burns of both lower legs".
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].
